 The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/),
 and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).
 
+## [Unreleased]
+
+### Fixed
+
+- Native wrappers that survive until global destruction release their
+  cache, reusable return scalar and JIT resources before Perl's final SV
+  sweep. This avoids reading freed values during CV magic cleanup on both
+  conventional and reference-counted stacks. A child-process regression
+  checks complete interpreter shutdown under several fixed hash seeds.
+
+- Reading a callback member from Perl with `PERL_RC_STACK` no longer
+  frees the wrapper's arguments and result prematurely. The call from get-magic
+  uses a separate non-reference-counted stack for its legacy stack operations.
+
 ## [v1.4.0] - 2026-10-31
 
 ### Fixed
